                <pb facs="0172" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg64"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 8.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports the killing, from the machine-gun firing directed on the
                    previous day on Rio de Janeiro, of several noncombatants and of a young woman
                    who was standing in front of the consulate of the United States. He transmits
                    the information, which still lacks confirmation, of the recapture of Catharina
                    Island by the Government forces.</p>
            </div>
